-- CHO Appointment & Enrollment System — MySQL 8.0 schema entry point
--
-- The authoritative, version-controlled schema lives in mysql/migrations/.
-- Do not edit this file to change the schema. Add a new numbered migration
-- instead so that every environment records the same history.
--
-- Fresh database or existing database:
--   npm run db:migrate
--
-- Check what is applied or pending:
--   npm run db:migrate:status
--
-- Verify database readiness (connection, tracking table, required tables,
-- utf8mb4 collation, pending migrations):
--   npm run db:verify
--
-- The runner creates the database tracking table `schema_migrations` and
-- applies mysql/migrations/*.sql in version order. It never creates or drops
-- the database itself, and it refuses to run a migration whose recorded
-- checksum no longer matches the file.
--
-- For a manual DBA review, read the files in mysql/migrations/ in order:
--   0001_initial_schema.sql
--   0002_query_indexes.sql
--
-- See docs/DATABASE_MIGRATION.md for the full procedure.
